[1.962189,"o","\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[3J contained **47 Codex threads plus 21 code-mode threads**, before tool descendants.                                     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n The exact native environment showed:                                                                                   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | Item | Observation |                                                                                                 \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n |---|---|                                                                                                              \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | Process limit | `RLIMIT_NPROC`: 461,771 soft/hard |                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | Address-space limit | Unlimited |                                                                                    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | Stack limit | 8 MiB soft; unlimited hard |                                                                           \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | File-descriptor limit | 1,048,576 |                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | Shell/bridge Node | Real ELF binary, **v24.13.0** |                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | Node selected by `disco` | Real ELF binary, **v24.20.0**, selected through the Lab’s configured PATH |               \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | TLS overrides | `NODE_OPTIONS`, `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`, `NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA`, `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED`,         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n `SSL_CERT_FILE`, `SSL_CERT_DIR`, `OPENSSL_CONF` and `OPENSSL_MODULES` all unset |                                      \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | Thread/loader overrides | `UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE`, `LD_PRELOAD` and `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` unset |                           \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n The Node difference follows the [normal `disco` launcher](/home/drew/.local/share/tangle-tools/deploy/disco:37); it    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n does not establish a version defect. In [Node v24.20.0’s                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n source](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v24.20.0/src/crypto/crypto_context.cc#L1004), the exact warning follows a  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n failed `uv_thread_create`. It reports failure to create the CA-loader thread—not certificate rejection. The bundled    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n [libuv thread-pool code](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v24.20.0/deps/uv/src/threadpool.c#L244) can abort after   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n thread-creation failure, consistent with exit 134; the precise abort stack remains unknown.                            \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n **Smallest durable fix:** the **cli-bridge resource owner**, through the **braid launcher**, should size the dedicated \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n bridge’s native-scope budget for its supported Codex/code-mode/tool concurrency using the existing                     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n `CLI_BRIDGE_SCOPE_TASKS_MAX` setting. Keep finite containment and TLS verification. The evidence establishes that 128  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n failed; it does not justify an exact replacement value. The owner’s completion check should capture peak tasks and     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n verify zero PID refusals under the intended reader concurrency.                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n The existing launcher documents an earlier task-exhaustion/EAGAIN incident. The Lab catalog also contains sandbox      \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n PID-exhaustion evidence, but that does not establish Chromium or zombie acc"]
[1.962289,"o","umulation here.                             \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n Your successful direct-SSH reader is consistent with execution outside this scope. My independent SSH comparison       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n stopped at **host-key verification failure**; I did not bypass it. No readers were retried, and no deployment, limits, \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n credentials, profiles or runs were changed.                                                                            \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;119;166;255m›\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;225;230;240mprofile discovery-operator\u001b[39m · \u001b[38;2;225;230;240mrunner codex\u001b[39m · \u001b[38;2;225;230;240mmodel gpt-6.1-sol\u001b[39m · \u001b[38;2;225;230;240mbackend Discovery operator on GTR\u001b[39m              \u001b[38;2;112;211;151mcompleted\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[?2026l"]
